= The Red Front Fighters' League

The Proletarian Hundreds were banned in the autumn of 1923, and the Nazis and the Bavarian leagues did not stop. In July 1924 the party's first Red Front Fighters' League groups appear in the cities. They march in uniform, protect meetings, and say they are open to all workers, not just party members. Ernst Thälmann will lead the federal organisation from February 1925.

What the League is for is not settled. A shield for meetings is a different organisation from an army for the next October.

- @mass: Make it a mass organisation open to all workers.
- @army: Make it a disciplined paramilitary force.

